## 1.2.1

```
HUD scrolling - switching to a Grimoire spell from the HUD list no longer makes the list flicker, and the list scrolls smoothly again, also on dedicated servers.
HUD Switch Delay - new setting (250 ms by default): a Grimoire spell is equipped once the HUD cursor has stayed on it that long, so scrolling past spells swaps nothing. Set it to 0 to equip each spell as the cursor reaches it. In the F3 window and on the mod's page.
HUD counts - the spell you just switched away from no longer shows x0 for a moment.
```

## 1.2.0

```
Docking - the grimoire now docks to Better Spells' settings window through Kiln. The two stay together with no lag, and nothing flashes when one key opens both. Hold Shift while dragging to move one alone, and drop it back beside the other to join them again. Needs Better Spells 1.3.0 and Kiln 0.2.0-dev.31.16 or newer.
Window - Kiln now remembers where you left the grimoire, starting from the place you already had.
Older Kiln - before Kiln 0.2.0-dev.31.16, the grimoire opens where you left it, without docking.
```

## 1.1.0

```
Multiplayer - Grimoire now works on dedicated servers and when you join someone else's world, not only in worlds you host. The server (or the host) needs Grimoire too, and so does each player who wants a grimoire. Dedicated servers haven't been tested in game yet.
Multiplayer - each player has their own grimoire, order and settings. Players without Grimoire are left alone.
Better Spells - with Better Spells 1.2.0 installed, the grimoire and its settings window open side by side, even on the same key, and move together while they touch. Hold Shift while dragging to move one alone. Needs Kiln 0.2.0-dev.31.11 or newer.
Window - opened alone, the grimoire still opens where you left it.
```

## 1.0.0

```
First release.
```
